ry is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. Its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05ec37a8f4fd33c05a2438df5c5fbc697f8b560fde0b9fe73922a0db56a09c2c.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[y]_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{{x}^{4}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535935 17592186045417 true] [17592186351412 1074 "![](images/d5/d5d777577f85cd577ce35bfd3a99c1e2218622d1856f4fe7ee4afe1cfd2c9f86.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 8,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. Its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05ec37a8f4fd33c05a2438df5c5fbc697f8b560fde0b9fe73922a0db56a09c2c.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int